8. What run() does
   run() is the real frontend executor for the report.

   It:
   - checks that at least one metric is selected
   - expands/collapses the filter box UI
   - builds the dynamic DataTable column definitions
   - builds the report table HTML
   - collects selected filters
   - expands custom ad sizes
   - posts all parameters to:
     - /admin/reports/fetch_platform_stats
   - enables server-side DataTables processing
   - shows or hides export depending on returned data

9. Admin AJAX endpoint
   AJAX request handler:
   - fetch_platform_stats($format = 'json')
   File:
   - app/application/modules/admin/controllers/reports.php

   It reads and sanitizes:
   - interval
   - timezone
   - from_date
   - to_date
   - metrics
   - advertiser
   - campaign
   - creative
   - publisher
   - site
   - adblock
   - country
   - adsize
   - revtype
   - dimensions

   It uses helper:
   - clean_data()
   From:
   - app/application/helpers/utilities_helper.php

   Then it:
   - sets page = PLATFORM_REPORT
   - sets display_type = TABLE
   - sets stat_type = PLATFORM for AJAX mode
   - converts CSV values into arrays
   - injects interval into dimensions when interval is not CUMULATIVE
   - merges metrics and dimensions into columns
   - forwards DataTables search, paging, sorting, and request payload

10. API controller entry
   Admin controller posts to:
   - api/v1/report/fetch

   API controller file:
   - app/application/modules/api.v_1/controllers/report.php

   The real API entry function is:
   - fetch_post()

   This function is important because it is the actual dispatcher for the report flow.
   It was missing from earlier documentation.

11. What fetch_post() does
   fetch_post() performs the shared reporting orchestration.

   It:
   - validates api_key in __construct()
   - detects account type
   - converts MANAGER to ADMIN reporting scope
   - gets agency_id for admin/manager context
   - loads reporting configuration
   - reads datatable_obj
   - builds search, group, order, and limit structures
   - parses timezone into UTC offset
   - converts date_from and date_to from selected timezone into UTC
   - applies page-specific search filters
   - converts DataTables sorting via convert_sorting_data()
   - routes by stat_type

12. PLATFORM routing
   Inside fetch_post(), for:
   - stat_type = PLATFORM

   The API routes to:
   - do_report->fetch($columns, $search, $group, $order, $limit, $dataTable, $page)

   Important note:
   There is also a method named:
   - fetch_platform(...)
   in do_report.php

   But the current admin Platform Reporting flow does not call that method.
   It uses the shared:
   - fetch(...)
   path.

13. Query builder layer
   Main model:
   - app/application/modules/api.v_1/models/do_report.php
   Main method used:
   - fetch($columns, $search, $group, $order, $limit, $dataTable = FALSE)

   Base data table:
   - rv_data_summary_ad_hourly as oxah

   The method:
   - builds a dynamic SELECT list from chosen metrics and dimensions
   - creates date/time expressions with timezone conversion
   - joins advertiser-side tables when needed
   - joins publisher-side tables when needed
   - applies filters
   - applies grouping
   - applies ordering
   - applies DataTables paging
   - returns either DataTables rows or raw records

14. Important joins used by fetch()
   Depending on selected dimensions/filters, fetch() joins:
   - rv_banners as oxb
   - rv_campaigns as oxc
   - rv_clients as oxcl
   - rv_zones as oxz
   - djax_site_zone_assoc as dsza
   - djax_publisher_sites as oxps
   - rv_affiliates as oxaff
   - djax_conf_revenue_type as dcrt

15. Filters applied in fetch()
   The query can filter by:
   - advertiser account
   - campaign
   - creative
   - publisher account
   - site
   - adblock
   - country
   - adsize
   - revenue type
   - environment/device
   - date range
   - DataTables search text
   - agency scope

16. Grouping and interval logic
   Grouping depends on selected dimensions and interval.

   Examples:
   - If interval = HOUR, fetch_platform_stats() prepends HOUR into dimensions and the query exposes DATE + HOUR
   - If interval = MONTH, results group by month
   - If interval = CUMULATIVE, no interval dimension is forced

17. Timezone logic
   Timezone is handled in two places:

   In API controller:
   - selected local date range is converted to UTC before querying

   In model:
   - grouped date/time columns use CONVERT_TZ(...) so displayed DATE, HOUR, MONTH, YEAR values match the selected timezone

18. Special page-specific behavior
   Platform Reporting has a special condition in do_report->fetch():
   - some zone-size filtering logic is skipped when page = PLATFORM_REPORT

   This is one of the important platform-report-specific behaviors.

19. DataTables response
   For table mode, API fetch_post() returns DataTables JSON containing:
   - sEcho
   - iTotalRecords
   - iTotalDisplayRecords
   - aaData
   - overview_chart_data

   The current widget uses:
   - aaData
   to fill the dynamic table

   A container for chart output exists:
   - #container-outcome

   But this widget does not contain active code that renders overview_chart_data into a Highcharts chart.

20. Export flow
   Export button handler:
   - jQuery('#save_search').on('click', ...)

   It:
   - validates at least one metric
   - copies current filter state into hidden fields
   - submits form to:
     - /admin/reports/generate_zip

   Backend export method:
   - generate_zip($type = FALSE)
   File:
   - app/application/modules/admin/controllers/reports.php

   For Platform Reporting, generate_zip() calls:
   - fetch_platform_stats('php')

   In export mode, fetch_platform_stats():
   - sets stat_type = EXPORT
   - sends empty DataTables search values
   - calls the same API endpoint again
   - returns decoded raw result data

   generate_zip() then:
   - prepares PHPExcel
   - builds headers from interval, dimensions, and metrics
   - fills rows from the returned dataset
   - outputs the report as Excel download

